{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1535233-two-questions-lamia-kith-and-intelligence-attacks","id":1535233,"title":"Two Questions: Lamia Kith and Intelligence Attacks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-07T17:16:22-07:00","id":1535233,"title":"Two Questions: Lamia Kith and Intelligence Attacks","content":"I had two questions.<br /> 1. Does anyone have an opinion on what the seeming/kith would be for a naga or a lamia (a human torso and a snake tail)? It seems like all the changelings are fairly humanoid in shape so I wasn't sure how to design something without legs.<br /> 2. Does anyone know a way to inflict damage using Intelligence or Wits? Attacks and Contracts always seem to require you to use Strength and Dexterity or sometimes Presence to inflict damage. I just thought it felt a little odd that a game that explicitly has magic in it, doesn't have anyway for a brainy character to take advantage of his brains in a fight. He still needs to invest in physical attributes to be able to do any damage to his enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28466-darkling235","name":"darkling235","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-07T19:24:29-07:00","id":1535239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>darkling235</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1535233-two-questions-lamia-kith-and-intelligence-attacks#post1535233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had two questions.<br /> 1. Does anyone have an opinion on what the seeming/kith would be for a naga or a lamia (a human torso and a snake tail)? It seems like all the changelings are fairly humanoid in shape so I wasn't sure how to design something without legs.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would depend entirely on what the kith is supposed to represent and do. Even setting aside Kith and Kin's note that kiths represent the mythic and iconic rather that mere professions or descriptors, kiths that are just descriptions of anatomical curiosity are liable to flop \u2014 there's a reason the Cyclopeans have not specifically hung their hat on having one eye.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Does anyone know a way to inflict damage using Intelligence or Wits? Attacks and Contracts always seem to require you to use Strength and Dexterity or sometimes Presence to inflict damage. I just thought it felt a little odd that a game that explicitly has magic in it, doesn't have anyway for a brainy character to take advantage of his brains in a fight. He still needs to invest in physical attributes to be able to do any damage to his enemies. </div> </div> </div>Changeling being &quot;a game that explicitly has magic in it&quot; doesn't really have any bearing on this absence. Fae magic is not an intellectual pursuit to such a degree that their interface with the world inside people's heads uses Social Attributes. By the same token, Mental Attributes generally correspond to activities that don't immediately translate to damage that will affect a mobile living being.<br /> <br /> Short of homebrewing Court or Goblin Contracts (or Independent Contracts or a new Regalia), the ways you leverage your Mental Attributes to deal damage is through setup, and even then that's likely to still require you or somebody else to make a roll with other stats; Being good at interacting with the world will often entail more than quick thinking and memory, especially if, as I suspect to be the case, you're talking about dealing damage at a scale likely to help decide a violent conflict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}